Chapter: EncodeJsonEscapes

 CCE has no code point for backspace, formfeed, carriage return or tab, so
 RFC 8259's four named escapes have no literal answer here and this chapter
 pins the one we chose instead of the one the spec asks for. Until 2026-08-25
 all four were handed to the encoder as from-unicode's -1 sentinel and came
 back as the single unit 255, which reads as an ordinary letter rather than a
 corruption: three distinct escapes collapsed onto one plausible wrong value
 and no fixture in the tree spelled any of them.

 A tab keeps its whitespace intent as a space. Backspace, formfeed and
 carriage return are teletype and line-printer machinery and are dropped. An
 unmappable \uXXXX is content rather than machinery, so it is refused.

  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Encode chapter Json

Section: Probe

  units : Text, Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  units (t) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else units t (i + 1) n (acc & " " & show (char-code-at t i))

  verdict : Maybe JsonValue -> Text
  verdict (m) =
    when m
     is Just (v) -> "JUST"
     is None -> "REFUSED"
    end

  body : Maybe JsonValue -> Text
  body (m) =
    when m
     is Just (v) -> inner v
     is None -> "refused"
    end

  inner : JsonValue -> Text
  inner (v) =
    when v
     is JsonStr (s) -> "len=" & show (text-length s) & " units=" & units s 0 (text-length s) ""
     is otherwise -> "not a string"
    end

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line ("plain  " & body (json-parse "\"ab\""))
    print-line ("bs     " & body (json-parse "\"a\\bb\""))
    print-line ("ff     " & body (json-parse "\"a\\fb\""))
    print-line ("cr     " & body (json-parse "\"a\\rb\""))
    print-line ("tab    " & body (json-parse "\"a\\tb\""))
    print-line ("lf     " & body (json-parse "\"a\\nb\""))
    print-line ("u0041  " & body (json-parse "\"a\\u0041b\""))
    print-line ("u00C0  " & body (json-parse "\"a\\u00C0b\""))
    print-line ("u0007  " & verdict (json-parse "\"a\\u0007b\""))
    print-line ("u000D  " & verdict (json-parse "\"a\\u000Db\""))
    print-line ("bad    " & verdict (json-parse "@@@"))
  end

